  "taxes_and_fees": {
    "_note": "Applied after Total Electric Charges. On the validated bill these came to $9.72 of $110.97 (~9%). All three bases were derived arithmetically from one bill and match to the cent — see rates/VALIDATION.md.",
    "state_regulatory_fee_per_kwh": 0.001,
    "state_regulatory_fee_source": "Schedule E-PUC, 'Surcharge to Fund Public Utilities Commission Reimbursement Fee', $0.001 per kWh for all service, Advice Ltr. 4763-E effective Jan 1 2026. Applies to all tariff rate schedules.",
    "franchise_fee_differential_pct": 5.78,
    "franchise_fee_differential_applies_to": "customers within the corporate limits of the City of San Diego",
    "franchise_fee_differential_base": "total_electric_charges - pcia - wf_nbc",
    "franchise_fee_differential_base_excludes_cca_generation": "On a CCA account 'total electric charges' is SDG&E's own total and stops above the CCA generation section. Schedule NEM-ST SC 3(c) requires the separation: 'The charges or credits resulting from a CCA's generation services shall not be co-mingled with charges or credits resulting from services provided by the Utility.' Verified against the net-exporter bill: 24.60 fixed + 7.12 NBC net of wildfire = 31.72 x 5.78% = 1.83, the figure printed.",
    "franchise_fee_base_pct": 1.1,
    "franchise_fee_base_source": "Preliminary Statement, General Information H.1 (EGENERAL, tarfKey 1), Advice Ltr. 3326-E effective Jan 1 2019: the Franchise Fee Differential is 'the difference between the franchise fee percentage and 1.1%'. So 1.1% is the base franchise fee everywhere in the territory, and a city's total is 1.1% plus its differential.",
    "franchise_fee_equivalent_surcharge_pct": 6.88,
    "franchise_fee_equivalent_surcharge_pct_DEPRECATED": "Kept for reference only — the engine now derives the rate as franchise_fee_base_pct + the city's differential. 6.88% is that derivation for the City of San Diego (1.1 + 5.78) and was never a territory-wide constant; applying it everywhere overcharged every customer outside San Diego by 5.78 points on this line.",
    "franchise_fee_equivalent_surcharge_applies_to": "CCA customers only — the utility imputes its own Schedule EECC and charges franchise fees on that commodity amount (Schedule CCA, per D.97-10-087). Entities of the State of California or a political subdivision are exempt.",
    "franchise_fee_equivalent_surcharge_base": "imputed_sdge_eecc + care_surcharge",
    "franchise_fee_equivalent_surcharge_unverified": "The 6.88% rate is NOT published in Schedule CCA or CCA-CRS — it appears to be city-set. Taken from the bill. The base derivation (imputed EECC + CARE surcharge at 0.00437/kWh) reproduces the bill's 65.44 exactly, but is inferred from a single bill, not stated in any tariff.",
    "franchise_fee_equivalent_surcharge_rate_VARIES_BY_CITY": "CONFIRMED city-set by a second bill: a CEA customer in a different city was charged 1.10%, against the 6.88% on the SDCP bill this figure came from. The BASE formula held up — the derived base came within 2.5% of that bill's printed 56.82 — but the rate is not a constant. The calculator applies 6.88% to everyone, which overstates this line for any city with a lower rate. Needs a city-to-rate mapping or a user input; see README 'Needs verifying'.",
    "care_surcharge_per_kwh": 0.00437
  },
